# Example ReRDMFT input file: He, cc-pVDZ, FUNCTIONAL PCCD, 4-component with the min-max stage, SPEED_OF_LIGHT 20.
#
# For two electrons pCCD (one electron pair) is exact once the orbitals are optimized, so this is the reference for
# casscf_he_c4_minmax.inp (CASSCF over the full orbital space, an independent implementation): the two agree to 2e-10 Hartree.
# SPEED_OF_LIGHT 20 makes the electron-positron relaxation visible (8.6e-7 Hartree; at the real c it is ~1e-10).
#
# Converged total energies:
#   no-pair (positive-energy-only) minimum: -2.8933945876 Hartree
#   min-max (including the negative-energy spinors): -2.8933937307 Hartree
NELEC 2
BASIS he-cc-pvdz.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
FUNCTIONAL PCCD
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG TRUE
MINMAX_ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO
SPEED_OF_LIGHT 20
USE_RI FALSE

GEOMETRY
He  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
END
